From: Uke contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: scope failed OPEN cleanup to its graph

The protected speaker runtime belongs to backend40. A failed OPEN of another
graph currently calls the provider removal callback, permanently rejecting
subsequent provisioning with ENODEV and erasing the speaker state. Use the
graph-scoped release callback instead. A failed speaker OPEN still mutes and
erases its calibration, marks Fault and retains the failed graph ID. Failed
OPEN IDs remain quarantined until provider removal, including non-speaker IDs.

Report the failed graph ID and errno without logging packet or calibration
contents. This is needed to distinguish the observed DSP duplicate response
from the later speaker failure; physical audio acceptance remains separate.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -111,7 +111,9 @@
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		/* Retain the ID until removal; remote ownership may be ambiguous. */
 		graph->state = ret;
-		q6apm_fs19xx_shutdown(apm);
+		q6apm_fs19xx_release(graph);
+		dev_err(apm->dev, "Graph %u OPEN failed: %d; ID quarantined\n",
+			graph_id, ret);
 		return ERR_PTR(ret);
 	}
 
